\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844  }{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 When do organizational people indulged themselves in organizational politics? Discuss any five factors in detail.}{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 
\par }{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par }{\cf2\ulc0\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 Answer: 
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 Organizational politics are actions that allow people in organizations to attain goals without goi
ng through ceremonial channels. Whether political activities help or hurt the organization depends on whether the person's goals are steady with the organization's goals. In the impartial model of organizations, people are assumed to manage sensibly, base
d on clear information and well-defined goals.
\par 
\par There are few factors that result in political activities in an organization  and are explained as under.
\par 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 1.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls2\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
Changes in Leadership}{\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844  which changes conventional associations and processes can create an opportunity for increased political behavior.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 2.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls2\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
Changes in Coordination and integration}{\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844  of organizational activities used to achieve common goals can also lead to an increase in political behavior.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 3.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls2\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
Changes in any of the five contextual forces, i.e. }{\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 environment, technology, strategy, culture, and structure, can generate uncertainty over resource allocation, leading to an increase in political behavior. 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls2\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
Blame & Integration.}{\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844  Blaming and attacking others to deflect attention from one's mistakes and using ingratiating behavior to gain favor are unethical and negative types of political actions.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 5.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls2\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7820760 {\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
Building Relationship}{\f1\cf2\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 . People develop relationships through coalitions, grouping, networks, and accommodating managerial linkages. Coalitions are relationships forme
d over specific issues. Alliances are general agreements of support among different individuals and groups; and networks are broad, loose support systems. Relationship building can either help or harm the organization.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid7820760\charrsid1732844 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844     }{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 Question No: 54    ( Marks: 10 ) 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid3694950\charrsid1732844 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1078{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}
{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}\picscalex100\picscaley100\piccropl0\piccropr0\piccropt0\piccropb0\picw15584\pich26\picwgoal8835\pichgoal15\wmetafile8\bliptag-1895836859\blipupi-161{\*\blipuid 8effd34580ace9d478c35331c42d728e}
010009000003b500000005001c00000000000400000003010800050000000b0200000000050000000c020d006c0e040000002e0118001c000000fb029cff0000
000000009001000000000440001254696d6573204e657720526f6d616e0000000000000000000000000000000000040000002d01000004000000020101000500
00000902000000020d000000320a5a00ffff01000400ffff0000670e0d0020f32d00030000001e0008000000fa0200000600000000000000040000002d010100
07000000fc020100000000000000040000002d0102000800000025030200040003005f0e030008000000fa0200000000000000000000040000002d0103000700
0000fc020000ffffff000000040000002d01040004000000f0010100040000002701ffff1c000000fb021000070000000000bc02000000000102022253797374656d000000000000fd99807c58bd1e0010f9230070bb1e005ae78339040000002d010100030000000000}}{
\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844  }{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 In order to get advantage of each method, will it be a sensible decision to simultaneously}{\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844  }{
\f1\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 apply all the four methods of job evaluation?}{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11893064\charrsid1732844 
\par }{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
\par }{\f1\cf2\ulc0\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 Answer: 
\par }\pard \ql \li540\ri566\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin566\lin540\itap0\pararsid11679424 {\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 Four methods of Job evaluation
\par 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 1.\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1260\ri566\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1260\faauto\ls3\rin566\lin1260\itap0\pararsid11679424 {\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
Ranking Method: }{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
Raters examine the description of each job being evaluated and assemble the jobs according to their value to the corporation. This technique requires a team characteristically composed of both management and employee delegate to arrange job in a simple ra
nk order from uppermost to lowest. The most noticeable restraint to the ranking method is its utter lack of ability to be managed when there are a large number of jobs.}{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 2.\tab}Classification Method: }{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 A job evaluation method by which a number of classes or rating
s are defined to explain a group of jobs is known as categorization method. The classifications are created by identifying some common denominator skills, knowledge, }{\f1\cf2\insrsid14507131\charrsid1732844 and responsibilities}{
\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844  with the desired goal being the criterion of a number of distinctive classes or grades of jobs.}{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 3.\tab}Factor Comparison Method }{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
Raters need not keep the entire job in mind as they evaluate instead, they make decisions on separate phases, or issues, of the job. A basic fundamental hypothesis is that there are five universal job 
factors:  (1) Mental Requirements (2) Skills (3) Physical Requirements (4) Responsibilities 5) Working Conditions. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f1\cf2\ulc1\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.\tab}}{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 Point Method: }{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
Raters assign numerical values to specific job components, and the sum of these values provides a quantitative appraisal of a job\rquote 
s relative significance. The point method requires selection of job factors according to the nature of the specific group of jobs being evaluated. After determining the group of jobs to be studied, analysts conduct job analysis and write job descrip
tions. Next, the analysts select and define the factors to be used in measuring job value and which become the standards used for the evaluation of jobs. Education, experience, job knowledge, mental effort, physical effort, responsibility, and working con
ditions are examples of factors typically used.}{\f1\cf2\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid11679424\charrsid1732844 
\par }}